A clean industry-style API design would be:

                         clicKart APIs
                              │
             ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
             │                │                │
          PUBLIC            USER             ADMIN
             │                │                │
             ▼                ▼                ▼
        Auth APIs        User APIs        Admin APIs
        Product APIs    Cart APIs        Product Mgmt
        Category APIs   Order APIs       Category Mgmt
        Search APIs     Address APIs     Order Mgmt
1. PUBLIC APIs

These don't require login.

Authentication
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/auth/register	Register customer
POST	/api/auth/login	Login and receive JWT
POST	/api/auth/refresh	Refresh JWT, if implemented
Product browsing
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/products	Get products
GET	/api/products/{id}	Get product details
GET	/api/products/active	Get active products
GET	/api/products/category/{categoryId}	Products by category
GET	/api/products/search?name=laptop	Search products
Categories
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/categories	Get categories
GET	/api/categories/{id}	Get category

So a guest can do:

Browse products
Search products
View categories
View product details
Register
Login
2. USER APIs

These require:

Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
User Profile
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/users/me	Get logged-in user's profile
PUT	/api/users/me	Update profile
PATCH	/api/users/me/password	Change password
DELETE	/api/users/me	Deactivate/delete account

I recommend /me rather than:

/users/{id}

for customer self-service APIs because the JWT already identifies the logged-in user.

3. USER ADDRESS APIs
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/users/me/addresses	Add address
GET	/api/users/me/addresses	Get my addresses
GET	/api/users/me/addresses/{id}	Get one address
PUT	/api/users/me/addresses/{id}	Update address
DELETE	/api/users/me/addresses/{id}	Delete address

Later we can add:

PATCH /api/users/me/addresses/{id}/default

for setting the default shipping address.

4. CART APIs

Cart belongs to the logged-in user.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/cart	Get my cart
POST	/api/cart/items	Add product to cart
PUT	/api/cart/items/{productId}	Update quantity
DELETE	/api/cart/items/{productId}	Remove product
DELETE	/api/cart	Clear cart

Example:

POST /api/cart/items
{
    "productId": 10,
    "quantity": 2
}
5. USER ORDER APIs

Users should only see their own orders.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/orders	Place order / checkout
GET	/api/orders	Get my orders
GET	/api/orders/{id}	Get my order details
POST	/api/orders/{id}/cancel	Cancel my order
GET	/api/orders/{id}/tracking	Get tracking information

Later, depending on the payment design:

POST /api/orders/{id}/payment

could initiate payment.

6. USER PAYMENT APIs

Payment should be separated from normal order CRUD.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/payments/create	Create payment
GET	/api/payments/{id}	Get payment status
POST	/api/payments/{id}/verify	Verify payment

But the exact endpoints depend on which gateway we integrate.

7. USER AI CHATBOT APIs
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/chatbot/chat	Send message to AI
GET	/api/chatbot/history	Get chat history
DELETE	/api/chatbot/history	Clear chat history

Example:

{
    "message": "Show me laptops under 60000"
}

The backend can then use:

ChatbotService
      ↓
AI API
      ↓
ProductService
      ↓
ProductRepository
      ↓
MySQL
8. ADMIN APIs

Now the important part.

Admin APIs should be protected with:

ROLE_ADMIN
ADMIN — Dashboard
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/dashboard	Dashboard statistics
GET	/api/admin/dashboard/sales	Sales statistics
GET	/api/admin/dashboard/orders	Order statistics
GET	/api/admin/dashboard/users	User statistics

Later we can add date filters:

/api/admin/dashboard/sales?from=2026-09-01&to=2026-09-26
9. ADMIN — Product Management

Admin can perform full CRUD.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/admin/products	Create product
GET	/api/admin/products	Get all products
GET	/api/admin/products/{id}	Get product
PUT	/api/admin/products/{id}	Update product
DELETE	/api/admin/products/{id}	Delete product
PATCH	/api/admin/products/{id}/status	Activate/deactivate
PATCH	/api/admin/products/{id}/stock	Update stock

This is different from public:

GET /api/products

because public users shouldn't have access to admin operations.

10. ADMIN — Category Management
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
POST	/api/admin/categories	Create category
GET	/api/admin/categories	Get all categories
GET	/api/admin/categories/{id}	Get category
PUT	/api/admin/categories/{id}	Update category
DELETE	/api/admin/categories/{id}	Delete category
PATCH	/api/admin/categories/{id}/status	Activate/deactivate
11. ADMIN — User Management
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/users	Get all users
GET	/api/admin/users/{id}	Get user
PUT	/api/admin/users/{id}	Update user
DELETE	/api/admin/users/{id}	Delete/deactivate user
PATCH	/api/admin/users/{id}/status	Enable/disable user
PATCH	/api/admin/users/{id}/role	Change user role

For example:

PATCH /api/admin/users/15/role
{
    "role": "ADMIN"
}

This endpoint must be heavily protected.

12. ADMIN — Order Management

Admin needs access to orders across the system.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/orders	Get all orders
GET	/api/admin/orders/{id}	Get order
PATCH	/api/admin/orders/{id}/status	Update order status
PATCH	/api/admin/orders/{id}/payment-status	Update payment status
POST	/api/admin/orders/{id}/cancel	Cancel order

Example:

PATCH /api/admin/orders/101/status
{
    "status": "SHIPPED"
}
13. ADMIN — Inventory

For a real e-commerce project, inventory deserves its own API.

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/inventory	View inventory
GET	/api/admin/inventory/low-stock	Low-stock products
PATCH	/api/admin/inventory/{productId}	Update stock

Example:

GET /api/admin/inventory/low-stock

could return:

[
    {
        "productId": 10,
        "productName": "iPhone 17",
        "stockQuantity": 4
    }
]
14. ADMIN — Payment Management
Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/payments	All payments
GET	/api/admin/payments/{id}	Payment details
GET	/api/admin/payments/failed	Failed payments
POST	/api/admin/payments/{id}/refund	Refund payment

Actual refund processing will happen through the payment gateway.

15. ADMIN — AI Chatbot

Admin might eventually need:

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/admin/chatbot/analytics	Chatbot usage
GET	/api/admin/chatbot/conversations	View conversations
GET	/api/admin/chatbot/feedback	Chatbot feedback